1. Problem and Users

The platform supports our research team in turning raw research material into reliable handbook pages about AI for SMEs. Research information can come from many different sources, such as reports, websites, statistics and interviews. The platform should help us process this information in a consistent and efficient way.

The primary users are the student research team who create the handbook. The secondary users are SME owners and managers who read the final handbook. For them, the information should make AI easier to understand and help them decide whether certain AI developments or applications are relevant to their business.

2. What the Platform Must Let a User Do

The platform should support the complete research process from raw source material to a published handbook page. Users should be able to collect and add sources, check whether they are relevant, reliable and recent, and process both Dutch and English material. Dutch sources should be translated into English without losing the original meaning.

After the sources have been processed, the platform should help select the most important findings and turn them into a structured first draft. The research team must always be able to manually review, correct and approve the content before it is published on the existing handbook site. In this way, the platform supports the researcher instead of fully replacing human judgement.

3. Output Qualities

A good handbook page produced by the platform should be clear, accurate, relevant and practical. The language should be understandable for SME owners without specialist knowledge of AI. Important claims should be supported by reliable and recent sources so that the information can be trusted.

The page should also give a balanced view of AI by explaining both opportunities and possible risks or limitations. Most importantly, the information should be useful in practice. An SME owner should understand what the findings mean for their organisation and what a possible next step could be.

4. Known Constraints

The platform will be developed by directing an agentic CLI instead of building the system completely by hand. We will reuse the existing handbook website and wiki rather than creating new infrastructure.

The platform must be usable by a non-coder, so users should be able to run the research workflow through clear instructions without needing programming knowledge. Every automated step must also have a manual fallback in case the platform or an agent cannot complete the task.

The platform must work with both Dutch and English source material. It should be able to retrieve, translate and assess Dutch sources, such as CBS, the Chamber of Commerce, sector organisations, regional news and Dutch interviews. This ensures that language does not determine who on the team can perform the research.
